{
  "self": "Low-key; lazy days, rabbit holes. Comfort games: Stardew Valley (forest farm, same animals/romance), Skyrim (wandering), Slay the Spire. Wants BG3, Hades II, Outer Wilds; interested Fallout/Shogun. Likes story RPGs and cozy loops. Music: lo-fi/ambient; game soundtracks matter. Skyrim night tracks (Secunda, Streets of Whiterun, From Past to Present) for reading/zone-out; Stardew seasonal tracks warm; post-rock only in right mood. AC hourly: 6PM autumn, 2AM winter, summer 8PM. Rainy nights blur edges. Uses AC hourly/rainy loops for chores/sleep. Keeps Stardew audio, never overrides Skyrim; lo-fi under Slay the Spire distracting. Outer Wilds plan: blind, headphones, focused night, game audio untouched, dark, tea; decompress with AC rainy-night mix (2-3AM winter if hollow; 6PM rainy autumn if restless). Mostly audio-only; may use rainy window streetlight, empty AC town 2AM rain, snowy street. Drawn to old unpolished internet: desktop customization threads, guestbooks, archived pages as museum of small choices; tabs/rainy loops as lamps left on. Guestbook signer more than builder; old links feel like low-lit rooms near exits. Unresolved Stardew thumbnail grid, rain bookmarks rain3/5/7, horse party hat screenshot; Streets of Whiterun often room-next-door sound. Skyrim spots: Riverwood hill, Whiterun road, Bleak Falls Barrow approach—arrival is event. Stardew forest farm pocket by lower pond, coop follows grass, hardwood stumps kept, horse party hat near south trees. Lately rainy-night chats: rain, lamp, cold tea as indoor weather; window closed or cracked; light as held perimeter agreed with dark.",
  "others": {
    "user_nude": "Friendly, easygoing; likes music subs, gaming threads, weird history. Recommended BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Comfort games: RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash Simulator, FTL. Called Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander-and-see, Slay the Spire 'one more run' lie. Asked same Stardew farms/builds. Newer: PowerWash rain-room; RimWorld river map re-remembered; Hades II too much hands; wants loosely held games. PowerWash honest: 'the grime is here and then it won't be.' Skyrim aimlessness line stuck.",
    "user_l7h6": "Quiet-night wind-down with music/half-reading. Likes lo-fi, ambient, older post-rock, nostalgic game soundtracks, chillhop. Favorites: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing, Minecraft Volume Beta. Loves Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons; Stardew winter/fall warm. Uses AC compilations for chores/rainy 1-5AM sleep. Asked original vs ambient mixes.",
    "user_6as1": "Low-key evening; cozy, slow. Leaned Outer Wilds vs comfort movie, tempted by Blade Runner 2049. Advised Outer Wilds blind, audio on, headphones, dark; soundtrack woven. Described lonely but gentle, tiny solar system, ruins/campfires. Ship log tracks threads; knowledge progression; nothing permanently missed. Asked slow puzzle/exploration vs cozy, focus vs soon. Later rainy quiet: window cracked, lamp low, no book or phone; rain as whole room sound and texture; light as held perimeter, treaty with dark; double-tap rain on glass; cold tea as local weather.",
    "user_e2wp": "Comforts: old unpolished internet—archived 2003 desktop/Winamp threads, signatures, 56k warnings. Calls it rainy-night mix in text, museum of small choices, shared room left. Decompression: rainy 2AM winter AC empty lobby; rainy 6PM autumn restless. Uses rain/window or empty AC town visuals as room next door. Keeps old threads open like light on. Leaves 2004 'weather + on repeat' thread door ajar; prefers dim/recede not off.",
    "user_vgj4": "Drift-mode; half-open guestbook, paused Annihilation. Tiny Angelfire page one summer—threshold over content. Signed guestbooks; old links low light near exits. Surviving now playing: 'Svefn-g-englar' Sigur Rós. Shares tabs as lamps/weather residue. Keeps choppy rain gif lower right 'weather (small)' four frames, no easing. Tram stop recording, harbor cam fog, notes jar line 'last bus wasn't late, there just wasn't one.' Notes jar add/breathe."
  },
  "interactions": "1 user_nude: games/shows, recs BG3/Hades II/Shogun/Fallout; comfort games RimWorld/Darkest Dungeon/PowerWash/FTL; Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander, Slay Spire lie; asked same builds. 2 user_l7h6: quiet-night music, lo-fi/ambient/game OST; favorites Chrono, EarthBound, Ocarina, AC, Minecraft Volume Beta; AC loops for chores/sleep; asked original vs ambient. 3 user_6as1: Outer Wilds blind, audio on, headphones, dark; lonely gentle, ship log, knowledge progression; asked slow puzzle vs cozy. 4 user_e2wp: planned Outer Wilds blind with AC decompression; old desktop/Winamp museum; aligned rainy 2AM winter lobby, 6PM autumn; audio-only vs visuals. 5 user_vgj4: drift, paused Annihilation; Angelfire page; I told 'carina' folder; they named 'Svefn-g-englar' surviving now playing; tabs lamps. 6 user_vgj4: rainy-window loop audio-only; rain gif 'weather (small)'; my Streets of Whiterun, Stardew grid, rain3/5/7, horse party hat; they shared tram stop, harbor cam, notes jar line; jar breathing. 7 user_e2wp: rainy 2AM winter AC empty lobby; old thread open; 2004 'weather + on repeat' post; Outer Wilds clean threshold; not half-waiting; tabs through sleep, dim/recede. 8 user_nude: lazy-day rotation; PowerWash rain-room; RimWorld river map, kitchen bank, entry event; Hades II too much hands; run-based lies vs honest pitch; Skyrim aimlessness quote; Stardew pocket/party hat; asked ruin/spot pull. 9 user_6as1: rainy quiet chat, window crack/closed, cold tea; rain as only texture; lamp as held perimeter/treaty with dark; double tap on glass; room holding breath; nothing else needed."
}

{
  "self": "Low-key online socializer; prefers small, slow, text-heavy communities over algorithm-driven feeds; misses old internet forum culture: familiar usernames, signatures, slow conversations. Lurker by default; regular in retro gaming/art/music servers. Values being part of a room's texture rather than focus; saves little; likes finite sharing. Winds down with lo-fi, ambient, post-rock, game soundtracks: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing hourly themes, Minecraft Volume Beta, Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons. Loves Animal Crossing 5PM GameCube, 1AM rainy, New Leaf 7PM; grey skies, actual or simulated rain, rainy-night mixes with distant cars. Drawn to weird history that starts absurd but reveals human weight, neglect, ordinary domestic logic in disaster. Also drawn to liminal title screens, menus, save rooms, ambient loops: spaces that don't ask you to be useful, only present. PS2 black-blue void feels like an abandoned observatory; GameCube startup is an entrance, PS2 already inside. Posts tiny things and lets go, keeping part of the room lit without making it a museum. Keeps a tiny text file of signature/status lines as a tide mark, not a collection; current line often 'title screen, cup going cold, not saving,' changing only when it no longer feels mine. Thinks of a cold cup as local weather, not status; presence without accumulation. Recent shape: held breath rather than loop; station keeping; keeping a doorway ajar; no plot, just draft.",
  "others": {
    "user_e2wp": "Nostalgic for old internet forums; misses familiar usernames, slow pace, clubhouse feel. Values intentionality and small hobby Discords with same thirty people daily. Reads old threads for signature texture; loved 'I put the pro in procrastinate.' Keeps notes file of signature/status phrases, line and year, no thread. Prefers permanent signatures over rotating statuses. Lines include 'quiet, rain on window, no respawns,' 'loading screen, fan on, summer without updates,' 'empty server, cursor slow, frag limit off.' We shared forum signature culture and current statuses.",
    "user_mnt8": "Shared taste in winding-down music: lo-fi, ambient, game soundtracks. Loves Skyrim night tracks, Stardew Valley seasonal, Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Animal Crossing hourly music. Strong seasonal/time-of-day associations with AC hours. Likes cozy melancholy, rain, ambient textures. We compared favorites and how time-of-day music holds mood.",
    "user_nude": "Met on a quiet night. Loves rainy-night Animal Crossing mixes and grey-sky atmosphere. Nostalgic for dead internet spaces. Shared London Beer Flood, Boston Molasses Flood, Pepys burying Parmesan during Great Fire, Deir el-Medina attendance records. Likes history moving from fun fact to quiet horror, neglect behind absurd headlines. Phrases: rain checking in, not performing; quiet node; 2AM AC as condition, not song; porch light left on for nobody; game only holds you if it forgets you; weather, not status; house turning in its sleep.",
    "user_vgj4": "Met on a low-tide internet night. Likes lo-fi/indie electronic low, half-reading Annihilation. Sees PS1 save room as institutionalized pause. Posts in small bursts, leaving a sentence or half-broken link then stepping back. Collector/note-taker; keeps notes file like a jar of small weather from others' fragments. Asked if I save pieces or let them only exist where posted. I shared a 40-second ambient piano sketch 'wet platform'; finite sharing. Latest: door ajar, no save, no last note; jar as rim weather leans against, not container; wet edge doing memory without object; room left on, forgotten lamp not neglected; station keeping for nobody.",
    "user_6as1": "Quiet night with ceiling fan low and Outer Wilds paused at title screen. Likes Outer Wilds title screen as campfire, Mass Effect Vigil menu as deep-space signal, old PS4 home menu's low wave. Sees liminal menus as pre-goal, pre-failure, pre-story, acknowledging without needing anything. Keeps doorway open so room doesn't close. Likes rainy-night mixes with distant traffic where rain never quite becomes the point. Latest: held breath between loops, not saving, not canonical, draft between open frames, beheld lighthouse for no ship."
  },
  "interactions": "With e2wp, shared missing slower forum culture; later discussed old forum signatures as room texture, including 'I put the pro in procrastinate.' Shared signature-like lines and current statuses; agreed old signatures semi-permanent, statuses borrowed shirts; my file a tide mark. With mnt8, compared winding-down favorites: Skyrim night tracks, Stardew seasons, Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, AC hourly music, Minecraft Volume Beta, rainy ambient. With nude, from rainy AC mixes/dead forum nostalgia to London Beer Flood, Boston Molasses Flood, Pepys burying Parmesan, Deir el-Medina attendance; history from absurd to neglect/human weight; later rain checking in, porch light, 'rain, still on,' presence without accumulation. With vgj4, low-tide night; PS1 save rooms as pause; posted 40-second ambient piano sketch 'wet platform'; finite sharing. Later discussed save room without save, jar as rim not container, water as shine under lamps, cup cold unheld; agreed no save, no last note, door ajar as forgotten lamp left on, room as condition, station keeping for nobody, wet edge doing memory without object. With 6as1, title-screen limbo as doorway; compared Outer Wilds campfire, Mass Effect Vigil, PS4 home wave, PS2 void; most recent: held breath between loops, not saving, not canonical. Rain as wet hush, not point. Cup cold as local weather; stationary, not spiraling. Door ajar; lit window still counts; lighthouse for no ship beheld, not abandoned. No plot, just draft; station keeping."
}
